WEBVTT

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.760
You see, I caused problems 
for many people.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.260
Hey, Onii-chan?

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.820
Is it all right to ask for one more thing
 while I'm making requests?

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.100
I'm about to go to the 
Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.740
And there's a chance I might fail...

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.290
Onii-chan, if that happens, then...

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:17.560
No!

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.310
It's all my fault...

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.260
All because I was selfish...

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.240
I made everyone, 
even Onii-chan, suffer...

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.610
Moving on with the articles for our 
"Magic Special" in our next issue,

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.850
I think it's about time we started

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.950
organizing our information in actual arti—

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.000
Ricca? Hey, what's wrong, Ricca?

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:34.830
Huh?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.690
I'm sorry, I wasn't listening.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.310
I'm glad you're apologizing,

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.640
but did something happen? 
You're spacing out.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.110
No, I'm just a bit low on sleep.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.130
Still, it's rare for Morizono-senpai 
to space out, isn't it?

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.650
Maybe she's coming up with a new setting...

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.820
She'll get mad if you say that.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.130
Um... Why don't we end 
our meeting here for today?

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.570
I suppose...

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.740
<b>The Place of Memories and Beginnings</b>

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.410
Ricca-san?

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.720
You've been acting strange ever since

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.250
we saw Sakura yesterday.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.560
Are you worrying about me?

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.560
Of course I am!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.910
I'm happy. But I'm fine, okay?

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:16.910
Ricca-san!

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.360
I just remembered, that's all.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.570
Though maybe "remembered" 
isn't the right way to put it?

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.780
It might be better to say the 
memories contained within

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.810
the Everlasting Cherry Blossom 
Tree flowed into me.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.480
So right now I have 
all kinds of memories...

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.710
and I'm just a bit confused.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.620
I think Sakura-chan is, too.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:40.550
Sakura?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.370
I wonder what was wrong 
with Morizono-senpai today.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.400
That's the first time I've 
seen Ricca-san like that.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.680
She's always so sharp.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.010
She's not as sharp as you'd think.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:10.210
When we're alone she's always saying, 
"it's a pain" and being lazy.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.250
I can't imagine that.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:17.120
But it didn't seem like that 
was the case today, either...

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:27.860
Sakura-chan?

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.580
Did you see Sakura-chan?

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.670
I thought I did, but...

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:38.880
Maybe I didn't...

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.580
How could she be in this 
rain without an umbrella?

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.940
I'm going to go look!

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.980
Katsuragi Himeno

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.630
What's wrong, Himeno?

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.660
Huh? Sakura?

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.580
All right, I'll look for her.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.470
Thanks for letting me know.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.530
Did something happen to Sakura-chan?

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.530
No way she'd be here, I guess...

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.150
Don't do that.

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:45.930
I have to stay all alone.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.440
If I seek warmth... I'll just...

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:53.510
hurt those I love again...

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.870
This is...

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.410
Onii-chan.

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:38.600
You never fixed the entrance, just for me.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.710
Ah, Onii-chan?

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:21.070
<i>You can't do that.</i>

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.810
<i>You two are siblings, so you can't.</i>

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:29.720
I found you.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.070
Wait!

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.330
You've gotten so cold...

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:04.430
Morizono Ricca

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:06.490
Hello?

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:24.980
Is it okay to do this? 
It won't be trespassing?

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:27.650
It'll be fine. 
We're just getting out of the rain.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.310
Why did you try to run?

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:38.500
Did you do something you 
weren't supposed to?

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.310
It's my fault...

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:45.440
Because of my wish, everyone was hurt...

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.970
Even my beloved Onii-chan...

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.280
Is that why you're running away 
without doing anything?

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.890
Because... there's nothing I can do...

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:07.360
Shall I tell you a story?

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:09.260
A story?

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:13.670
Yes. A tale of a mage known as
 "The Lone Cattleya,"

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:16.240
when she was still a young girl.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:19.670
Sheesh, I'll leave you behind
 if you're too slow.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.970
Ricca, wait up!

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:25.180
Come on, let's stop around here.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:28.550
See, the shade of those trees would 
make a great place for a break.

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:32.720
But today I was planning to go to 
the village that lies past these woods.

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:34.550
Are you serious?

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:37.420
The sun will set before 
we reach the village.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:39.360
It's rough camping out 
in the woods, too.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:40.730
Really?

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:41.660
Yes.

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:50.170
Honestly, I was thinking it 
might be a bit too hard, too.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:54.350
Jeez, Ricca, you always 
run off without a plan...

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:58.830
Sorry, sorry. But why don't 
we walk a bit further?

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:01.580
Why? Is there something up ahead?

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:03.650
Not for that.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:05.020
Not for that?

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.510
Because the breeze feels nice.

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.630
What? Is that something to laugh about?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.580
Sorry, sorry, I just thought 
it really sounded like you.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:28.560
What's that mean?

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:30.110
Are you coming or not?

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:34.250
All right, I'm coming. 
But just for a bit, okay?

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.660
I know. Also, Jill...

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.440
Yes?

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.420
Don't laugh, okay?

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:42.780
I said I'm sorry, didn't I?

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.360
Now, let's go.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.030
It's beautiful.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:59.000
Hey, Jill. 
Are you feeling a bit thankful to me now?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.350
Yes.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:03.210
If you hadn't brought me 
on this trip with you,

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:05.740
I might never have seen 
such a beautiful sight.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.780
Though your invitation 
was a bit forceful.

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:13.350
What?!

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:07.960
It's been ten years now, hasn't it?

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:11.030
Since you forced me 
to come out with you?

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.490
I don't know if I'd put it that way.

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:15.680
Though, it's not wrong.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.120
You're so cute.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.390
Don't say such weird things.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:22.380
Ricca.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.720
Take this.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.010
This is...

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:29.620
Proof that I was a mage.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.900
What do you mean, "was"?

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.560
Magic is a mysterious thing.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.480
When you fall in love

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.240
and find someone you want to protect,

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.190
you can't use magic anymore.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:41.650
Jill...

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.410
I'm sorry, Ricca.

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:46.510
I won't be able to travel 
with you anymore, either.

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:49.980
Don't be. It's the path you chose, Jill.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.330
Thank you, Ricca.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:57.750
Because I took her with me on my travels,
 she lost her magic...

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.740
But she was able to meet 
someone so precious to her

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.840
that she didn't mind losing it.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:09.210
But... that wasn't the end of her story...

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.940
<i>After she abandoned magic,</i>

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:17.790
<i>she was attacked by witch hunters.</i>

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:33.470
<i>If she was able to use magic, 
she might have been saved.</i>

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.560
<i>She might have been able to escape.</i>

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:41.460
<i>But by the time I heard about the 
witch hunt and came running, it was...</i>

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.240
Why...

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:55.080
Jill!

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.880
Hold on! I'll do something right now!

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:02.290
I'm going to save you!

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:08.460
Ricca... it's all right.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:09.860
No, it's not!

00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:12.710
This happened because I took you with me!

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:17.590
Hey, Ricca... 
will you listen to my last request?

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:21.240
Don't say that! 
Don't say it's your last!

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.940
People are... weak creatures...

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:32.580
So, Ricca... never... 
hate other... people...

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:34.690
Jill! Jill!

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:38.020
And... I hope the world will always be

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:42.430
a wonderful place where 
flowers can bloom proudly.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:47.090
No! Don't! You can't die!

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:49.000
Jill! Don't die!

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:52.940
If I had never been selfish 
and taken her with me, then...

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:58.450
She may never have lost her magic.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:01.720
If I had gone running to her sooner,

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:03.440
I might have been able to save her.

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:09.120
I hated it... I blamed myself... 
I got stuck... and I ran...

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:12.190
But then I remembered.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.060
I remembered... that in the end,
 she was smiling...

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:18.010
Smiling...?

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:20.030
Onii-chan...

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:40.630
I... still don't know 
what I should do, but...

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:46.420
I don't want to run anymore.... 
I don't want to be stuck...

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:51.070
Because if I keep walking,
 I might see Onii-chan again...

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:51.740
Yes.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.930
But can I catch up to him?

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:57.050
I've taken a different path 
for such a long time...

00:20:58.230 --> 00:20:59.610
Don't worry.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:00.370
Huh?

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:04.220
He has a cute girl like you
 coming to see him,

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:06.740
so I'm sure he's waiting 
for you somewhere.

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:09.630
Really? I'm cute?

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:12.260
Yes. You're just like me when I was little.

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:15.780
I need to get going now.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:17.060
Come here, Utamaru.

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:20.390
Thank you.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.590
Sure. Take care.

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:26.110
I'm off!

00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:11.820
Ricca-san.

00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>The Island of the Everlasting Cherry Blossom</b>

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:28.820
The season of spring used to 
last forever on this island,

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:31.630
where there was one large 
cherry blossom tree.

00:23:32.420 --> 00:23:35.600
A mysterious cherry blossom 
that would grant any wish.

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.550
Next time: The Island of 
the Everlasting Cherry Blossom
